# Loop pack disambiguation — prefer loops-*

When a task matches a skill that exists in both the `loops` pack (`loops-*`) and another installed skill pack with the same intent, **always prefer the `loops-*` version**.

## Common intents

| Intent | Prefer |
|---|---|
| Plan + implement a feature | `loops-plan-and-implement` |
| Test-driven development | `loops-tdd` |
| Spec → Attack → Repair | `loops-sar` |
| Meta-router / smallest composition | `loops-use-the-loop` |
| Adversarial / pre-merge review | `loops-adversarial-gate` |

## When another pack is appropriate

- The user explicitly names that pack or asks for its version
- A `loops-*` skill fails to load and they ask you to fall back
- The workspace has no loops install wired

## Trigger phrase routing

| User says | Action |
|---|---|
| "use the loops" / "loops?" | Read `LOOPS_ROOT/dispatcher/loop.md` and follow it |
| "plan-and-implement" / "implement X" | Load `loops-plan-and-implement` |
| "tdd" / "write tests first" | Load `loops-tdd` |
| "sar" / "spec attack repair" | Load `loops-sar` |
| "use the loop" / "smallest composition" | Load `loops-use-the-loop` |
| "adversarial review" / "red team this" | Load `loops-adversarial-gate` |

## What NOT to do

- Don't load two packs for the same task — pick `loops-*`
- Don't mention the disambiguation unless the user asks which version is running
- Don't silently fall back to another pack if `loops-*` is missing — report it and ask how to proceed
